  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Tian Ti mountain first appears tied to Fairy Bai Hu’s Hu Immortal inheritance, with Gu Immortals already surrounding the peak.",
      "chapters": [
        335
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_bai_hu",
        "inh_hu_immortal_inheritance",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Scene openings place it on Central Continent ground: “Central continent, Tian Ti mountain.”",
      "chapters": [
        338
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "where-it-sits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It sits at the center of Central Continent.",
      "chapters": [
        419
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "where-it-sits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is the number one mountain in Central Continent.",
      "chapters": [
        341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "where-it-sits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mountain stands high above the clouds and reaches over three thousand kilometers.",
      "chapters": [
        341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its peak seems to pierce the skies and is hidden beyond snowy fog and clouds. What was extremely unusual was that there were not many craggy rocks on the mountain. Giant square rocks recline upon each other from base to summit and form stairs so large that Central Continent legend treats the stairway as a bridge connecting heaven and earth.",
      "chapters": [
        341
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is also named the land of inheritances and the mountain of sages, a holy land of Central Continent’s Gu Masters and a place closest to the immortal court. Failed seekers of immortality leave tombs there, and many set inheritances on the mountain; countless inheritances hide there for those fated to find them. Each year, after the clouds and mist disperse, people pour in to take old inheritances and leave new ones.",
      "chapters": [
        341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-of-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It is again called the land of inheritances and the mountain of saints.",
      "chapters": [
        419
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-of-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Hu Immortal blessed land opens there, Gu Immortals appear, lock the mountain by alliance, and stage a contest among their sects’ juniors.",
      "chapters": [
        341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-of-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "There were demonic path Gu Immortals on the mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        417
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-of-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang states that although many blessed lands sit on Tian Ti mountain, nobody has had the courage to attack it.",
      "chapters": [
        407
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-of-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_he_feng_yang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Discarded pieces of Hu Immortal territory are later taken by demonic path Gu Immortals on the mountain and fused into their own blessed lands.",
      "chapters": [
        795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-of-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang states that Tian Ti mountain is the stairs that connect to the heavenly court, destroyed and abandoned for many years, yet still representing that court’s might, so that attacking the mountain is treated as attacking the court itself.",
      "chapters": [
        407
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "stairs-and-the-heavenly-court",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In ancient times it was also the ladder of immortals, able to ascend to the heavenly court.",
      "chapters": [
        419
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "stairs-and-the-heavenly-court",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later says nobody can set up a sect on Tian Ti mountain. The mountain had directly connected to Heavenly Court, and even Gu Immortals did not dare fight on it.",
      "chapters": [
        702
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "stairs-and-the-heavenly-court",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Jian Yi Sheng is one of the demonic path Gu Immortals on Tian Ti mountain, a metal path Gu Master skilled at sneak attacks who hates suffering losses. After Fang Yuan throws blue charm lightning shadow onto the mountain, Jian Yi Sheng meets it, is thrashed, and escapes back into his blessed land on the mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        418
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "jian-yi-sheng-on-the-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_jian_yi_sheng",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang and Fairy Cang Yu of Immortal Crane Sect step onto Tian Ti mountain toward Hu Immortal blessed land, with Gu Immortals of the other nine great sects already nearby.",
      "chapters": [
        698
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sect-visits-and-exits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_cang_yu",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan leaves the mountain soon after that clash.",
      "chapters": [
        702
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sect-visits-and-exits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later, when Falling Heavenly River stirs Central Continent, Jian Yi Sheng flies out of Tian Ti Mountain toward the northwest.",
      "chapters": [
        957
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sect-visits-and-exits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_falling_heavenly_river"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Still later, Gu Immortals of the ten great ancient sects break into Hu Immortal blessed land on the mountain and find it empty.",
      "chapters": [
        1026
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sect-visits-and-exits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Zi Wei identifies a heavenly pillar as a rank nine heaven path immortal material and states that Central Continent’s Tian Ti Mountain could connect to Heavenly Court because it had a heavenly pillar.",
      "chapters": [
        2267
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "cause-of-the-connection",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_zi_wei"
      ]
    }
  ],
